  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Cairn",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/17424/450x258/cairn-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1789243200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/17424-buy-cairn-pc-steam/",
      "user": "Oniawyn",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/28211529-1768374832.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Super fun and challenging, I love this game! You don't have to be into climbing to have fun playing Cairn. The graphics are absolutely stunning and the storyline is amazing!\n\n\n\nCairn is a fantastic climbing game, one of the best! :D"
    },
    {
      "game": "The Blood of Dawnwalker",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/15628/450x258/the-blood-of-dawnwalker-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1789243200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/15628-buy-the-blood-of-dawnwalker-pc-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-b598e8",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Wonderful RPG. A great surprise! The Blood of Dawnwalker looks absolutely stunning and runs incredibly smoothly on Ultra settings. The dark atmosphere, day/night system, and the completely different gameplay styles between human and vampire forms give the game a unique identity. Combat feels fresh, especially with directional blocking and attacks, and your choices actually have consequences. After my first few hours, this already feels like a proper RPG — something we don’t get often enough these days. Highly recommended! 10/10 so far."
    },
    {
      "game": "Marvel Vs. Capcom Fighting Collection: Arcade Classics",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/17085/450x258/marvel-vs-capcom-fighting-collection-arcade-classics-pc-game-steam-europe-cover.jpg?v=1789243200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/17085-buy-marvel-vs-capcom-fighting-collection-arcade-classics-pc-game-steam-europe/",
      "user": "gamer-995b5a",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Great collection, legendary games and solid ports.\n\n\n\nThough the addition of a description and short explanation of the game mechanics would have been nice. Like they did with the games included in the Capcom Arcade Stadium 1-2 games."
    },
    {
      "game": "Far Far West",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/20985/450x258/far-far-west-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1789243200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/20985-buy-far-far-west-pc-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-ae8c268",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Far West has honestly been a really fun experience so far. One of the biggest things I like about the game is how much there is to do. Between leveling up, unlocking and improving abilities, exploring, and just constantly having something to work toward, it gives you a reason to keep playing without feeling like you’re doing the exact same thing over and over.\n\nThe multiplayer is also a huge plus. Being able to play with a group of friends is great, but even jumping online with random players has been a good experience. The community has actually surprised me too. From what I’ve seen, a lot of experienced players are willing to help newer players learn the game instead of just leaving them to figure everything out on their own.\n\nI also really like the sense of progression. There’s always another upgrade, ability, or goal to work toward, so even after playing for a while it still feels like you’re accomplishing something.\n\nObviously no game is perfect, and there’s always room for more content and improvements, but Far 4 West already has a really solid foundation. It’s fun solo, even better with friends, and definitely one of those games where you can tell yourself you’re only getting on for an hour and suddenly realize you’ve been playing all night. \n\nDefinitely recommend giving it a try, especially if you enjoy multiplayer games with progression, exploration, and plenty of things to keep you busy.far"
    }
  ],
